    <p class="title is-5 mathjax">
      
        Evidence-Guided Recovery for AI <span class="search-hit mathjax">Agents</span> with Ambiguous Tool <span class="search-hit mathjax">Outcomes</span> and Partial Execution
      
    </p>
    <p class="authors">
      <span class="has-text-black-bis has-text-weight-semibold">Authors:</span>
      
      <a href="/search/?searchtype=author&amp;query=Zhu%2C+G">Genliang Zhu</a>, 
      
      <a href="/search/?searchtype=author&amp;query=Chen%2C+X">Xiaobo Chen</a>, 
      
      <a href="/search/?searchtype=author&amp;query=Wang%2C+Z">Ziyuan Wang</a>, 
      
      <a href="/search/?searchtype=author&amp;query=Wang%2C+C">Chu Wang</a>
      
    </p>
    
    <p class="abstract mathjax">
      <span class="has-text-black-bis has-text-weight-semibold">Abstract</span>:
      <span class="abstract-short has-text-grey-dark mathjax" id="2610.41453v1-abstract-short" style="display: inline;">
        Tool timeouts can leave AI <span class="search-hit mathjax">agents</span> facing ambiguous tool&hellip;
        <a class="is-size-7" style="white-space: nowrap;" onclick="document.getElementById('2610.41453v1-abstract-full').style.display = 'inline'; document.getElementById('2610.41453v1-abstract-short').style.display = 'none';">&#9661; More</a>
      </span>
      <span class="abstract-full has-text-grey-dark mathjax" id="2610.41453v1-abstract-full" style="display: none;">
        Tool timeouts can leave AI <span class="search-hit mathjax">agents</span> facing ambiguous tool <span class="search-hit mathjax">outcomes</span> and partial execution: an action may have failed, committed or remained in flight while other workflow steps have already completed. We formulate evidence-guided task recovery over approved obligations, provider capabilities and states compatible with public evidence. A shared admissibility check handles key expiry, <span class="search-hit mathjax">authorization</span> timing, dependencies and residual effects; a terminal certificate separates actual goal satisfaction from publicly supported safe completion. The known-model implementation combines standard observation-contingent planning with a separately implemented effect-history adjudicator. In a finite study of 37 assignments, planning and three active controls each certify 28 completions; four saved synthetic fee units incur additional computation. A preregistered assignment-held-out comparison then evaluates planning advice against evidence prompting with two local model bundles. Across 58 paired units in 19 previously developed task families, advice certifies 30 completions versus 9, a 36.2-percentage-point difference (exact family sign-flip p=0.0078), using 272 proposals versus 399. All 116 trajectories pass independent replay. Both models exhibit a positive completion difference. The comparison measures the evaluated advice interface under a common shield; search-versus-rule advice requires a separate matched comparison. Unknown and handoff <span class="search-hit mathjax">outcomes</span> remain explicit, with guarantees tied to the declared provider capabilities rather than arbitrary third-party exactly-once execution.
        <a class="is-size-7" style="white-space: nowrap;" onclick="document.getElementById('2610.41453v1-abstract-full').style.display = 'none'; document.getElementById('2610.41453v1-abstract-short').style.display = 'inline';">&#9651; Less</a>
      </span>
    </p>
    

    <p class="is-size-7"><span class="has-text-black-bis has-text-weight-semibold">Submitted</span> 30 October, 2026; 
      <span class="has-text-black-bis has-text-weight-semibold">originally announced</span> October 2026.
      
    </p>
    
    <p class="comments is-size-7">
      <span class="has-text-black-bis has-text-weight-semibold">Comments:</span>
      <span class="has-text-grey-dark mathjax">24 pages, 1 figure, and 10 tables. Includes a finite recovery model, model-facing confirmation study with two local-model bundles, independent replay, and an explicit provider-capability scope</span>
    </p>
    

    

    
