    <p class="title is-5 mathjax">
      
        Cross-Interface <span class="search-hit mathjax">Authorization</span> for AI Computer-Use <span class="search-hit mathjax">Agents</span>
      
    </p>
    <p class="authors">
      <span class="has-text-black-bis has-text-weight-semibold">Authors:</span>
      
      <a href="/search/?searchtype=author&amp;query=Zhu%2C+G">Genliang Zhu</a>, 
      
      <a href="/search/?searchtype=author&amp;query=Wang%2C+C">Chu Wang</a>
      
    </p>
    
    <p class="abstract mathjax">
      <span class="has-text-black-bis has-text-weight-semibold">Abstract</span>:
      <span class="abstract-short has-text-grey-dark mathjax" id="2610.41397v1-abstract-short" style="display: inline;">
        Computer-use <span class="search-hit mathjax">agents</span> act through graphical interfaces, command lines, APIs, scripts, and Model Context Protocol servers. A policy decision can be interface-invariant while its executable&hellip;
        <a class="is-size-7" style="white-space: nowrap;" onclick="document.getElementById('2610.41397v1-abstract-full').style.display = 'inline'; document.getElementById('2610.41397v1-abstract-short').style.display = 'none';">&#9661; More</a>
      </span>
      <span class="abstract-full has-text-grey-dark mathjax" id="2610.41397v1-abstract-full" style="display: none;">
        Computer-use <span class="search-hit mathjax">agents</span> act through graphical interfaces, command lines, APIs, scripts, and Model Context Protocol servers. A policy decision can be interface-invariant while its executable <span class="search-hit mathjax">authorization</span> is not: another route can bypass mediation, alter a security-relevant default, or commit after the <span class="search-hit mathjax">authorized</span> state has changed. We present a profile-bounded protocol for a fixed, versioned computer-use deployment. It enumerates effect-bearing routes and durable sinks, checks a route-to-sink enforcement cut, normalizes each concrete request to a canonical effect, issues a route-bound prepare ticket, and verifies the route, effect, grant, trace, profile, inventory, and authoritative state again at commit. A committed result requires an agreeing sink receipt. Under explicit assumptions, we prove profile-bounded refinement, matched-effect decision invariance, resistance to alternate-route laundering and declared cross-surface recomposition, commit-time state safety, and receipt-grounded <span class="search-hit mathjax">outcomes</span>.
  The reference profile registers 12 effect families, five interfaces, and 60 routes. Two structurally distinct runtime mappings produce 3,464 traces over 1,732 scenarios each: 960 commits, 2,312 denials, and 192 commits after re-preparation. An independent checker accepts every retained trace and pair and rejects 26/26 semantic regressions; coverage and normalizer suites reject 24/24 and 720/720 mutants; and 168/168 commit probes match their declared <span class="search-hit mathjax">outcomes</span>. A frozen-source audit passes 52 checks over 12 files from two independent hybrid runtimes and one public <span class="search-hit mathjax">authorization</span> substrate. Source-shaped adapter refinements commit 48/48 instrumented calls and reject 15/15 unbound cases. The resulting guarantees bind the declared profile and its effect semantics.
        <a class="is-size-7" style="white-space: nowrap;" onclick="document.getElementById('2610.41397v1-abstract-full').style.display = 'none'; document.getElementById('2610.41397v1-abstract-short').style.display = 'inline';">&#9651; Less</a>
      </span>
    </p>
    

    <p class="is-size-7"><span class="has-text-black-bis has-text-weight-semibold">Submitted</span> 30 October, 2026; 
      <span class="has-text-black-bis has-text-weight-semibold">originally announced</span> October 2026.
      
    </p>
    
    <p class="comments is-size-7">
      <span class="has-text-black-bis has-text-weight-semibold">Comments:</span>
      <span class="has-text-grey-dark mathjax">31 pages, 2 figures, and 7 tables. Includes formal results, two reference runtime mappings, mutation tests, commit-time race probes, source-shaped adapter checks, and a frozen external-source audit. Guarantees bind the registered deployment profile and declared effect semantics</span>
    </p>
    

    

    
