    <p class="title is-5 mathjax">
      
        WebAnything: From the Wild Web to Scalable <span class="search-hit mathjax">Agent</span> Environments
      
    </p>
    <p class="authors">
      <span class="has-text-black-bis has-text-weight-semibold">Authors:</span>
      
      <a href="/search/?searchtype=author&amp;query=Xie%2C+T">Tianci Xie</a>, 
      
      <a href="/search/?searchtype=author&amp;query=Cai%2C+Z">Zikun Cai</a>, 
      
      <a href="/search/?searchtype=author&amp;query=Zhang%2C+C">Chaoyun Zhang</a>, 
      
      <a href="/search/?searchtype=author&amp;query=Guo%2C+P">Pinxue Guo</a>, 
      
      <a href="/search/?searchtype=author&amp;query=Li%2C+B">Bingxuan Li</a>, 
      
      <a href="/search/?searchtype=author&amp;query=Zheng%2C+R">Rui Zheng</a>, 
      
      <a href="/search/?searchtype=author&amp;query=Yan%2C+H">Hang Yan</a>
      
    </p>
    
    <p class="abstract mathjax">
      <span class="has-text-black-bis has-text-weight-semibold">Abstract</span>:
      <span class="abstract-short has-text-grey-dark mathjax" id="2610.37786v1-abstract-short" style="display: inline;">
        Web <span class="search-hit mathjax">agents</span> require diverse, executable, and resettable website environments for reproducible training and evaluation. Human-assisted mirrors demand per-site engineering, while generative construction can diverge from specified real websites. Capture-and-replay preserves observations, with interaction coverage constrained by captured content and replay capabi&hellip;
        <a class="is-size-7" style="white-space: nowrap;" onclick="document.getElementById('2610.37786v1-abstract-full').style.display = 'inline'; document.getElementById('2610.37786v1-abstract-short').style.display = 'none';">&#9661; More</a>
      </span>
      <span class="abstract-full has-text-grey-dark mathjax" id="2610.37786v1-abstract-full" style="display: none;">
        Web <span class="search-hit mathjax">agents</span> require diverse, executable, and resettable website environments for reproducible training and evaluation. Human-assisted mirrors demand per-site engineering, while generative construction can diverge from specified real websites. Capture-and-replay preserves observations, with interaction coverage constrained by captured content and replay capabilities.
  We present WebAnything, a fully automated framework that reconstructs source-grounded, reusable Web environments from real URLs without per-site manual implementation or repair after initial setup and <span class="search-hit mathjax">authorization</span>. An Explorer-Builder collects browser-observable structures, resources, and interaction <span class="search-hit mathjax">outcomes</span>; an independent verifier checks frozen candidates and guides local repair or targeted source recapture.
  We construct 244 website artifacts across 14 application domains and 53 categories, supporting 12,984 executed and accepted tasks. Compared with human-assisted WebHarbor, WebAnything achieves higher aggregate scores on three fidelity metrics, with 12 wins, two ties, and no losses in a blind audit. Fine-tuning Qwen3.5-9B on 5,856 interaction trajectories improves REAL success by 9.9 percentage points, Odysseys-Easy Rubric Avg and Task Avg by 6.25 and 6.32 percentage points, and WebArena-Verified Overall success by 13.33 percentage points under the fixed harness. Code: https://github.com/china-qijizhifeng/Web-Anything
        <a class="is-size-7" style="white-space: nowrap;" onclick="document.getElementById('2610.37786v1-abstract-full').style.display = 'none'; document.getElementById('2610.37786v1-abstract-short').style.display = 'inline';">&#9651; Less</a>
      </span>
    </p>
    

