        A durable <span class="search-hit mathjax">agent</span> can resume a consequential action while its&hellip;
        <a class="is-size-7" style="white-space: nowrap;" onclick="document.getElementById('2610.31916v1-abstract-full').style.display = 'inline'; document.getElementById('2610.31916v1-abstract-short').style.display = 'none';">&#9661; More</a>
      </span>
      <span class="abstract-full has-text-grey-dark mathjax" id="2610.31916v1-abstract-full" style="display: none;">
        A durable <span class="search-hit mathjax">agent</span> can resume a consequential action while its <span class="search-hit mathjax">authority</span> changes and the action&#39;s external <span class="search-hit mathjax">outcome</span> remains uncertain. We study execution-time reliability of tool-using AI <span class="search-hit mathjax">agents</span>, isolating recovery decisions from language-model behavior. Checkpoint state, permission to dispatch, evidence of an external effect and permission to reconcile are distinct obligations. We present a finite conformance study that checks these obligations through histories scored against a provider effect ledger hidden from the recovering application. A prospectively frozen campaign executes 336 histories on native LangGraph and Temporal hosts, crossing 14 schedules, three provider contracts and four matched application policies. All 168 paired host cells have identical checked <span class="search-hit mathjax">outcomes</span>. Per host, retained-ledger reconciliation passes all 42 histories: 21 checked completions, 15 denials and six unknown <span class="search-hit mathjax">outcomes</span> with reservations retained. Cached retry, revalidation before retry and stable-key retry pass 30, 36 and 31 histories respectively. A separate 16-case component study of InfinityOS, an enterprise AI platform developed by Arya.ai, exercises exported <span class="search-hit mathjax">authority</span>, worker, recovery and settlement code over repository fakes. The results isolate the roles of current <span class="search-hit mathjax">authority</span>, provider contracts and retained observations in recovery, with safety, completion and unresolved obligations reported separately for the declared application profile.
        <a class="is-size-7" style="white-space: nowrap;" onclick="document.getElementById('2610.31916v1-abstract-full').style.display = 'none'; document.getElementById('2610.31916v1-abstract-short').style.display = 'inline';">&#9651; Less</a>
