    <p class="title is-5 mathjax">
      
        VeeReview: Measuring Build-Verify Pairs in <span class="search-hit mathjax">Agent</span>-<span class="search-hit mathjax">Authored</span> Pull Requests from a V-Model Perspective
      
    </p>
    <p class="authors">
      <span class="has-text-black-bis has-text-weight-semibold">Authors:</span>
      
      <a href="/search/?searchtype=author&amp;query=Dautovi%2C+G">Gabriel Dautovi</a>, 
      
      <a href="/search/?searchtype=author&amp;query=Wu%2C+J+J">Jie JW Wu</a>
      
    </p>
    
    <p class="abstract mathjax">
      <span class="has-text-black-bis has-text-weight-semibold">Abstract</span>:
      <span class="abstract-short has-text-grey-dark mathjax" id="2610.29143v1-abstract-short" style="display: inline;">
        Context: Reviewing a pull request requires verification evidence that addresses the proposed change. Coding <span class="search-hit mathjax">agent</span> benchmarks and studies of pull request&hellip;
        <a class="is-size-7" style="white-space: nowrap;" onclick="document.getElementById('2610.29143v1-abstract-full').style.display = 'inline'; document.getElementById('2610.29143v1-abstract-short').style.display = 'none';">&#9661; More</a>
      </span>
      <span class="abstract-full has-text-grey-dark mathjax" id="2610.29143v1-abstract-full" style="display: none;">
        Context: Reviewing a pull request requires verification evidence that addresses the proposed change. Coding <span class="search-hit mathjax">agent</span> benchmarks and studies of pull request <span class="search-hit mathjax">outcomes</span> do not directly assess this relationship. Objective: We test whether the V-Model&#39;s build and verify pairs can measure verification evidence in pull requests and support comparisons between <span class="search-hit mathjax">agent</span>-<span class="search-hit mathjax">authored</span> and human-<span class="search-hit mathjax">authored</span> changes. Method: VeeReview classifies four build and verify pairs using repository signals and a language-model judge. Three pairs use model judgements constrained by deterministic signals, and a rule over the diff and repository tree decides Module Design-Unit Test. We evaluated VeeReview against a 25-pull request reference set labelled by two raters and applied it to 1,454 matched pairs of <span class="search-hit mathjax">agent</span> and human pull requests from 741 repositories. Results: VeeReview assigned lower build-only rates to <span class="search-hit mathjax">agent</span>-<span class="search-hit mathjax">authored</span> pull requests on all four pairs, contrary to the preregistered hypothesis (mixed-effects odds ratios 0.52 to 0.86). Architecture-Integration was not significant. Standardization for linked issues, shipped tests and size reduced matched-rate differences by 34% to 60%, and the rule-decided pair&#39;s standardized interval included zero. The instrument did not meet its preregistered calibration criterion: agreement with adjudicated labels was 4% to 60% against a required 80%, and inter-rater agreement was weak (kappa = 0.154). Conclusions: The rule-decided pair shows that a process measure judged by a language model partly reflects how a pull request is presented rather than the verification work behind it. We report the cohort differences as observations made with this instrument, and we argue that such measures need a mechanically decided component and a validated human reference before they can support comparisons of verification practice.
        <a class="is-size-7" style="white-space: nowrap;" onclick="document.getElementById('2610.29143v1-abstract-full').style.display = 'none'; document.getElementById('2610.29143v1-abstract-short').style.display = 'inline';">&#9651; Less</a>
      </span>
    </p>
    

    <p class="is-size-7"><span class="has-text-black-bis has-text-weight-semibold">Submitted</span> 20 October, 2026; 
