    <p class="title is-5 mathjax">
      
        CXBench: A Benchmark for Process-Compliant LLM <span class="search-hit mathjax">Agents</span> in Regulated Customer-Experience Workflows
      
    </p>
    <p class="authors">
      <span class="has-text-black-bis has-text-weight-semibold">Authors:</span>
      
      <a href="/search/?searchtype=author&amp;query=Yu%2C+B">Boxi Yu</a>, 
      
      <a href="/search/?searchtype=author&amp;query=Zhang%2C+Y">Yuzhong Zhang</a>, 
      
      <a href="/search/?searchtype=author&amp;query=Su%2C+Z">Zhenfeng Su</a>, 
      
      <a href="/search/?searchtype=author&amp;query=Xi%2C+L">Linfu Xi</a>, 
      
      <a href="/search/?searchtype=author&amp;query=Yao%2C+Y">Yinghan Yao</a>, 
      
      <a href="/search/?searchtype=author&amp;query=Chen%2C+S">Shitao Chen</a>, 
      
      <a href="/search/?searchtype=author&amp;query=Cao%2C+Y">Yang Cao</a>, 
      
      <a href="/search/?searchtype=author&amp;query=Lin%2C+L">Liting Lin</a>, 
      
      <a href="/search/?searchtype=author&amp;query=Briand%2C+L">Lionel Briand</a>, 
      
      <a href="/search/?searchtype=author&amp;query=Mu%C3%B1oz%2C+E">Emir Muñoz</a>
      
    </p>
    
    <p class="abstract mathjax">
      <span class="has-text-black-bis has-text-weight-semibold">Abstract</span>:
      <span class="abstract-short has-text-grey-dark mathjax" id="2610.25954v1-abstract-short" style="display: inline;">
        Tool-using language <span class="search-hit mathjax">agents</span> increasingly perform regulated customer-service workflows, where a correct final state is insufficient:&hellip;
        <a class="is-size-7" style="white-space: nowrap;" onclick="document.getElementById('2610.25954v1-abstract-full').style.display = 'inline'; document.getElementById('2610.25954v1-abstract-short').style.display = 'none';">&#9661; More</a>
      </span>
      <span class="abstract-full has-text-grey-dark mathjax" id="2610.25954v1-abstract-full" style="display: none;">
        Tool-using language <span class="search-hit mathjax">agents</span> increasingly perform regulated customer-service workflows, where a correct final state is insufficient: <span class="search-hit mathjax">agents</span> must also provide disclosures, obtain consent, and follow required procedures. Existing tool-<span class="search-hit mathjax">agent</span> benchmarks largely score final business states, accepting trajectories that reach correct <span class="search-hit mathjax">outcomes</span> through non-compliant processes.
  We introduce cxbench, a benchmark that evaluates <span class="search-hit mathjax">outcome</span> and process compliance separately across six regulated domains. Each task combines a customer request, a tool-based environment, and explicit process requirements. Rule cards link cited regulatory obligations to observable trace evidence. A hybrid grader combines deterministic checks for ordering and <span class="search-hit mathjax">authority</span> with an LLM judge for semantic requirements. We define a false-pass as an <span class="search-hit mathjax">outcome</span>-pass run that fails process checks.
  Across seven models and 120 tasks, 55.5% of the 840 retained executions are false-passes, representing 80.1% of <span class="search-hit mathjax">outcome</span>-passing runs; only 13.8% pass both checks. Process-inclusive evaluation changes the observed model ordering and exposes differences hidden by <span class="search-hit mathjax">outcome</span>-only scoring. cxbench makes these failures inspectable through trace-linked criteria.
        <a class="is-size-7" style="white-space: nowrap;" onclick="document.getElementById('2610.25954v1-abstract-full').style.display = 'none'; document.getElementById('2610.25954v1-abstract-short').style.display = 'inline';">&#9651; Less</a>
      </span>
    </p>
    

    <p class="is-size-7"><span class="has-text-black-bis has-text-weight-semibold">Submitted</span> 19 October, 2026; 
      <span class="has-text-black-bis has-text-weight-semibold">originally announced</span> October 2026.
      
    </p>
    

    

    
