    <p class="title is-5 mathjax">
      
        SecODD: Adapting the Operational Design Domain from Driving Autonomy to Autonomous Cyber Defense
      
    </p>
    <p class="authors">
      <span class="has-text-black-bis has-text-weight-semibold">Authors:</span>
      
      <a href="/search/?searchtype=author&amp;query=Kang%2C+J">Jina Kang</a>, 
      
      <a href="/search/?searchtype=author&amp;query=Yun%2C+J">Jeong-Han Yun</a>, 
      
      <a href="/search/?searchtype=author&amp;query=Choi%2C+H">Hyesong Choi</a>
      
    </p>
    
    <p class="abstract mathjax">
      <span class="search-hit">Abstract</span>:
      <span class="abstract-short has-text-grey-dark mathjax" id="2610.24741v1-abstract-short" style="display: inline;">
        Security operations centers are beginning to delegate detection, triage, and containment to Autonomous Cyber Defense (ACD) <span class="search-hit mathjax">agents</span> at execution time. Erroneous high-impact playbooks can disrupt critical services and create accountability gaps among deployers, SOC supervisors, vendors, managed service providers, and infrastructure providers. We propose SecODD,&hellip;
        <a class="is-size-7" style="white-space: nowrap;" onclick="document.getElementById('2610.24741v1-abstract-full').style.display = 'inline'; document.getElementById('2610.24741v1-abstract-short').style.display = 'none';">&#9661; More</a>
      </span>
      <span class="abstract-full has-text-grey-dark mathjax" id="2610.24741v1-abstract-full" style="display: none;">
        Security operations centers are beginning to delegate detection, triage, and containment to Autonomous Cyber Defense (ACD) <span class="search-hit mathjax">agents</span> at execution time. Erroneous high-impact playbooks can disrupt critical services and create accountability gaps among deployers, SOC supervisors, vendors, managed service providers, and infrastructure providers. We propose SecODD, an execution-time governance framework for ACD that adapts the Operational Design Domain concept from autonomous-vehicle regulation to cyber autonomy. It defines the <span class="search-hit mathjax">authorized</span> scope of automated defensive actions, models when meaningful human intervention must remain possible, and specifies auditable due-care conditions through a Mitigation Safe Harbor. Four engineering requirements---tamper-evident logging, human-in-the-loop orchestration, rollback playbooks, and safe-state transition controls---are evaluated through a per-scenario audit matrix that illustrates how two ACD failure modes can be translated into pass/fail audit <span class="search-hit mathjax">outcomes</span>. The result is an evidence-oriented framework that <span class="search-hit mathjax">authorizes</span> ACD only when autonomous actions are bounded, interruptible, recoverable, and reconstructable from evidence.
        <a class="is-size-7" style="white-space: nowrap;" onclick="document.getElementById('2610.24741v1-abstract-full').style.display = 'none'; document.getElementById('2610.24741v1-abstract-short').style.display = 'inline';">&#9651; Less</a>
      </span>
    </p>
    

