    <p class="abstract mathjax">
      <span class="has-text-black-bis has-text-weight-semibold">Abstract</span>:
      <span class="abstract-short has-text-grey-dark mathjax" id="2610.22507v1-abstract-short" style="display: inline;">
        Command-line interface (CLI) <span class="search-hit mathjax">agents</span> increasingly execute longer-horizon tasks, yet existing benchmarks either assume that user instructions remain fixed throughout execution or evaluate task&hellip;
        <a class="is-size-7" style="white-space: nowrap;" onclick="document.getElementById('2610.22507v1-abstract-full').style.display = 'inline'; document.getElementById('2610.22507v1-abstract-short').style.display = 'none';">&#9661; More</a>
      </span>
      <span class="abstract-full has-text-grey-dark mathjax" id="2610.22507v1-abstract-full" style="display: none;">
        Command-line interface (CLI) <span class="search-hit mathjax">agents</span> increasingly execute longer-horizon tasks, yet existing benchmarks either assume that user instructions remain fixed throughout execution or evaluate task <span class="search-hit mathjax">outcomes</span> without capturing runtime collaboration quality. In this paper, we present REALCLI, a paired benchmark that unifies the evaluation of task execution and human-<span class="search-hit mathjax">agent</span> collaboration quality on realistic CLI tasks. To comprehensively measure collaboration, REALCLI builds a five-dimensional framework, operationalized into 22 sub-dimensions and 51 interaction scenario templates. REALCLI provides two modes for paired comparison: REALCLI-EXEC supplies complete specifications upfront, whereas REALCLI-COLLAB introduces a scripted user that delivers progressive information, corrections, constraint revisions, and <span class="search-hit mathjax">authorization</span> decisions. Evaluations reveal profound capability gaps in frontier <span class="search-hit mathjax">agents</span>: the best configuration attains an average score of only 49.2%, and when evaluated by the joint collaboration score ($J_{\mathrm{collab}}$), the peak performance reaches merely 37.6%. These results show that task effectiveness diverges sharply from collaboration quality, with models consistently struggling in steerability, trust calibration, and safety boundary management. REALCLI provides a rigorous, reproducible foundation for measuring and advancing collaborative CLI <span class="search-hit mathjax">agents</span>.
        <a class="is-size-7" style="white-space: nowrap;" onclick="document.getElementById('2610.22507v1-abstract-full').style.display = 'none'; document.getElementById('2610.22507v1-abstract-short').style.display = 'inline';">&#9651; Less</a>
      </span>
    </p>
    

