    <p class="abstract mathjax">
      <span class="search-hit">Abstract</span>:
      <span class="abstract-short has-text-grey-dark mathjax" id="2610.16357v1-abstract-short" style="display: inline;">
        <span class="search-hit mathjax">Agentic</span> video reasoning systems gather and assess video evidence across stages, selecting relevant spans as visual evidence for answering questions. New candidates and observations prompt reassessment of the current span, but revisions can correct localization errors or discard useful evidence already present in the adopted span. Systems therefore need to co&hellip;
        <a class="is-size-7" style="white-space: nowrap;" onclick="document.getElementById('2610.16357v1-abstract-full').style.display = 'inline'; document.getElementById('2610.16357v1-abstract-short').style.display = 'none';">&#9661; More</a>
      </span>
      <span class="abstract-full has-text-grey-dark mathjax" id="2610.16357v1-abstract-full" style="display: none;">
        <span class="search-hit mathjax">Agentic</span> video reasoning systems gather and assess video evidence across stages, selecting relevant spans as visual evidence for answering questions. New candidates and observations prompt reassessment of the current span, but revisions can correct localization errors or discard useful evidence already present in the adopted span. Systems therefore need to connect evidence organization across stages with temporal state control, allowing accumulated information to jointly inform revision assessment while explicit adoption decisions govern how assessment <span class="search-hit mathjax">outcomes</span> affect downstream visual evidence. We introduce VideoSlate, a stateful commit-control framework built around shared evidence. A typed evidence blackboard links candidate spans, provenance, construction, and verifier observations, enabling an incumbent-relative certifier to assess revision support from the candidate, current span, and related proposals. Based on certification, the controller <span class="search-hit mathjax">authorizes</span> a revision or retains the current span, separating evidence accumulation from state updates and recording each decision and its evidence on the blackboard. Extensive evaluations across video grounding and grounded question-answering benchmarks show that VideoSlate can improve temporal localization through selective revision.
        <a class="is-size-7" style="white-space: nowrap;" onclick="document.getElementById('2610.16357v1-abstract-full').style.display = 'none'; document.getElementById('2610.16357v1-abstract-short').style.display = 'inline';">&#9651; Less</a>
      </span>
    </p>
    

